  "conclusion": "No evidence for a safe newest-record-wins rule. Identical Bicester geometries have identical start/version timestamps. The large Graven Hill polygon has later start and version timestamps than several contained plots. Publisher says only latest polygon versions are published; distinct IDs can nevertheless arise when polygons change, split or merge. A stale or simplified current parent index extent following a subdivision remains possible, but not proven by these timestamps.",
